A||||1||Lynx||Is the 3.0 similar to the 2.8!
Z||000000||Lynx||06-23-99||01:14 AM||||I was just curious about the 3.0 that is in my moms 87 Pontiac Grand am. Are these engines anything like the 2.8 that came in the Fieros. I belive they only came out for 2 years but it had lots of power in my moms car. Well the engine blew (broken timing chain) and my dad replaced it with a used one and the blown one is still here and i was thinking about rebuilding it and making a swap into my Fiero. Just want to know what the differences is with it and the 2.8.<p>Lynx<p>Before you ask he replaced it because it bent valves and he didnt have time to rebuild it.
Z||000001||Hock||06-23-99||12:07 PM||||NO. The 3.0 and the 2.8 are totaly differant engines. The 3.0 is wider than the 2.8 and has less power(120 3.0 to 140 2.8). The 3.0 is also a heavier engine than the 2.8. So for any type of upgrade, as far as I have seen, the 3.0 would be a waste of time.
